preConditionHook:
// Leave on the first bar that is not another with-trend trend bar: the spike
// has stopped. The opposite trigger to ConsecutiveCloseExit, which leaves
// after a RUN of with-trend closes rather than the moment one fails to appear.
//
// This cannot be a trend-bar Entry rule placed negated in the exit pane -- an
// Entry rule cannot sit there, exactly as the catalog notes for
// ConsecutiveCloseExit -- so the negation is written into the rule.
//
// ctx.BarsSinceEntry() >= 1 stops the entry bar itself from triggering it, per
// the source's own note. BarsSinceEntry is 0 on the fill bar and 0 while flat
// (VERIFIED, never a -1 sentinel), so the guard also cannot fire when flat;
// the MarketPosition test is what picks the SIDE.
//
// Product, not quotient, for the body test: EL raises a runtime
// divide-by-zero and a zero-range bar is legal data. Deepest bar read is 0.
